      "id": "q",
      "kind": "question",
      "title": "Practice problem",
      "text": "Original teaching exercise.\nAn ideal Hooke spring is in static equilibrium within its linear elastic range. Its stiffness is k=200 N/m and the applied tensile force is F=10 N. Find the extension x under this steady load.",
      "refs": [
        {
          "document_id": "lesson",
          "page": 1
